BSP-Yocto-TISDK-AM68x-ALPHA1                    2023-05-26
==========================================================

- Linux TI vendor kernel v5.10.158 (based on TI tag 08.06.00.002)
  * Tag: v5.15.158-phy5
- U-Boot v2021.01 (based on TI tag 08.06.00.002)
  * Tag: v2021.01_08.06.00.002-phy6
- Yocto 3.1 (dunfell)

NOTE:
This is an ALPHA release and has not been tested for full functionality. It is
possible that some features are not working or stable. This release will NOT
be supported after the first full BSP release.


Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------

- tisdk-default-image:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-1


Build Environment:
------------------

- Ubuntu 18.04 64-bit


Features:
---------

- Added support for new machine:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-1
- Booting from MMC/SD, eMMC and UART (bootloader only) supported
- Support for the following features:
  * eMMC Flash
  * Micro SD Card
  * OSPI and QSPI Flash
  * EEPROM (2x SoM, 1x carrier board)
  * GPU
  * USB 2.0 + USB 3.0 5 GBit/s
  * MIPI-CSI with phyCAM-M: VM-016, VM-017 and VM-020
  * MIPI-DSI -> LVDS transceiver with AC-199 and AC-200 panels
  * 2x Ethernet
  * ePWM (including fan support)
  * I2C (including temperature sensors on SoM)
  * UART
  * User LEDs
  * RTC
  * CAN
  * ADC
  * TPS6594 pmic

Known Issues:
-------------
- MMC/SD is limited to 3.3v
- The MCU ethernet is limited to 100 MBit/s and booting is not possible
  due to a phy reset triggered from the MCU domain which is unknown to Linux
- The MIPI DSI interface swaps the RGB colors occasionally
- Displayport, PCIe and the I2C GPIO expander are not functional
